{"answer": "Volunteers encounter several obstacles when trying to meet CLC needs: securing and sustaining funding (grants are competitive and often not renewed, leading to financial uncertainty); limited community resources that overlook mental\u2011health priorities; difficulty keeping youth engaged amid school, jobs, and social pressures; challenges scaling support groups to reach more people; and broader logistical barriers, stigmatization, and a general lack of resources that hinder program planning and stability.", "event": "final_answer", "evidence_count": 5, "llm_called": true, "not_found": false, "query_id": "xdlihuno-q3::chain_hop::node27::attempt1", "ts_monotonic": 224188.349165756, "ts_unix": 1777954121.9243987, "worker_id": "node27"}
{"answer": "Volunteers encounter several challenges when trying to meet CLC (Community Learning Center) needs, including:\n\n- **Financial hardship:** Limited and uncertain funding, fierce grant competition, and lack of long\u2011term resources make planning difficult and threaten program sustainability.  \n- **Youth engagement:** Keeping young volunteers involved is tough because they must balance school, jobs, and social pressures.  \n- **Scaling support:** Expanding support groups to reach more people is difficult.  \n- **Mental\u2011health barriers:** Stigmatization and the tendency to overlook mental\u2011health needs when allocating scarce resources hinder volunteer efforts.  \n- **Logistical/resource constraints:** General lack of resources and logistical limitations further impede volunteers\u2019 ability to adapt to CLC demands.  \n\nThese points are drawn directly from the provided evidence; no conflicting values appear.", "event": "final_answer", "evidence_count": 5, "llm_called": true, "not_found": false, "query_id": "xdlihuno-q3::chain_hop::node27::attempt2", "ts_monotonic": 224196.951285356, "ts_unix": 1777954130.5265183, "worker_id": "node27"}
